  "description": "Frozen conformance vectors for the published check-decision table. Byte-identical copies live on both sides of the receipt: the issuer copy (@kaval/receipt-verifier) and the published mirror (@usekaval/kaval/verify). Two implementations that both pass these cannot disagree about any verdict, reason-code set, or refusal these cases cover — which is the only enforceable form of 'the customer runs the same table the issuer ran'.",
